Make_Car_Fly: contiguous rotation matrix + angle SVECTOR (scattered-locals class)

MulMatrix2((undefined4*)local_58, &local_38) and Calc_Object_Angles(&local_38,
(short*)&local_18) consume a 3x3 short matrix at [ebp-0x38..-0x26] and an 8-byte
angle SVECTOR at [ebp-0x18..-0x11] as single blocks; Ghidra declared them as 9+3
separate scalars, gcc scatters them -> scrambled matrix -> wrong flight vector.
This was the first real native/wasm state divergence of the L2 demo (cf121:
car2 flight field +0x72 = 0 native vs 0x4c wasm; watchpoint-proven writer
Make_Car_Fly's CONCAT22 store). _ang[3] is the SVECTOR pad published to car+0x74
straight from uninitialized stack even in the original; zero it for
deterministic cross-target state.

